# Exam track — Theme: Family & Myself — Sub-lesson 1: Vocabulary
# Sproochentest oral-exam topic. Target level ~B1 (authoring guideline only).
#
# Every sub-lesson mixes words AND sentences so each session alternates
# word-match and sentence-builder slots; the emphasis here is vocabulary.

@lesson F1.01 "Family Vocabulary"

# --- Close family ---
@word d'Famill = family
@word de Papp = father
@word d'Mamm = mother
@word d'Elteren = parents
@word de Brudder = brother
@word Bridder = brothers
@word d'Schwëster = sister
@word Schwësteren = sisters
@word Geschwëster = siblings
@word de Jong = son
@word d'Duechter = daughter
@word d'Kand = child
@word d'Kanner = children
@word de Mann = husband
@word d'Fra = wife

# --- Wider family ---
@word de Grousspapp = grandfather
@word d'Groussmamm = grandmother
@word d'Grousselteren = grandparents
@word d'Enkelkand = grandchild
@word de Monni = uncle
@word d'Tatta = aunt
@word de Cousin = cousin
@word d'Schwéiermamm = mother-in-law
@word de Schwéierpapp = father-in-law
@word de Frënd = friend

# --- Talking about yourself ---
@word den Numm = surname
@word de Virnumm = first name
@word d'Alter = age
@word de Gebuertsdag = birthday
@word d'Adress = address
@word de Beruff = profession
@word bestuet = married
@word leedeg = single
@word geschidden = divorced
@word jonk = young
@word al = old

# --- Doing things ---
@word wunnen = to live
@word schaffen = to work
@word heeschen = to be called

@sentence
@lu Meng Famill ass net ganz grouss.
@en My family is not very big.
@distractor-lu kleng
@distractor-lu seng
@distractor-en small
@distractor-en his

@sentence
@lu Ech wunne mat menger Fra zu Lëtzebuerg.
@en I live with my wife in Luxembourg.
@distractor-lu schaffen
@distractor-lu Mann
@distractor-en work
@distractor-en husband

@sentence
@lu Mäi Gebuertsdag ass am Mee.
@en My birthday is in May.
@distractor-lu Numm
@distractor-lu Juni
@distractor-en name
@distractor-en June
